{#
    The Fantasy admin screen's own styles, injected once per page.

    🚨 Separate from `front/styles`, deliberately. That sheet is ninety lines
    of league, draft and lineup styling that an administrator's browser has no
    use for, and pulling it in here to reach one rule would ship all of it on
    a page that renders none of it.

    🚨 Values come from Convoro's space scale. `--s-3` is 0.75rem, which is
    what these forms were spaced by before — written into each tag as a
    `style` attribute, where no stylesheet could find it and no theme could
    ever change it.
#}
<style>
/*
 * Each league's card is a short stack of single-action forms — rescore,
 * reschedule, adopt, delete — and each needs air above the one before it.
 *
 * Written as a sibling rule rather than a class on every form, because the
 * thing being described is the GAP BETWEEN them, not a property of any one.
 * The first form sits tight under the paragraph above it, every later one is
 * separated, and a fifth form added next year is spaced without anybody
 * remembering to say so.
 */
.admin-card-body > form + form { margin-top: var(--s-3); }
</style>
